This repository has not been initialised yet.

The presence of this file is what permits `.github/workflows/init-template.yml`
to run. That workflow rewrites the template author's identity to yours - the
licence holder, the funding target, the documentation footers, and the issue
chooser's contact link - and then deletes this file, which is what stops it
ever running again.

It should fire on its own shortly after generation. GitHub does not reliably
deliver an event when a repository is created from a template, so if nothing
happens, run "🎉 Initialise From Template" from the Actions tab. Running it
twice is harmless.

Deleting this file by hand skips initialisation entirely; you would then edit
LICENSE, .github/FUNDING.yml, and .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml yourself.
